WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.168
-My first guest is one of the
biggest names in country music,

00:00:03.168 --> 00:00:05.871
who just announced his
"Proud to be Right Here" tour,

00:00:05.871 --> 00:00:07.774
which kicks off July 8th.

00:00:07.774 --> 00:00:10.710
Please welcome Luke Bryan,
everybody!

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:12.779
Oh, great to see you, buddy!

00:00:12.779 --> 00:00:14.013
That's what I'm talking about.

00:00:14.013 --> 00:00:15.614
-What's up?

00:00:15.614 --> 00:00:17.082
-It is great to see you, buddy.

00:00:17.082 --> 00:00:19.018
Welcome back to the show.

00:00:19.018 --> 00:00:20.853
Congrats on this,
by the way, here.

00:00:20.853 --> 00:00:24.924
This is the deluxe version
of your album

00:00:24.924 --> 00:00:27.761
"Born Here, Live Here,
Die Here," which is out now.

00:00:27.761 --> 00:00:30.897
And soon, you're gonna be able
to perform these songs live,

00:00:30.897 --> 00:00:33.366
because you just announced
you're going on tour.

00:00:33.366 --> 00:00:35.968
-Then I'm gonna be able to put
the deluxe of the deluxe

00:00:35.968 --> 00:00:37.403
of the deluxe out.
-Of course,

00:00:37.403 --> 00:00:39.039
that's what we're all wait--
Exact-- Yeah.

00:00:39.039 --> 00:00:41.273
Or just release
a whole new album, yeah.

00:00:41.273 --> 00:00:42.641
The tour starts July 8th.

00:00:42.641 --> 00:00:45.277
Tickets are available
this Friday.

00:00:45.277 --> 00:00:48.248
What are you looking forward to
most about the tour?

00:00:48.248 --> 00:00:50.116
-Well, my thing is I keep --

00:00:50.116 --> 00:00:53.720
I keep thinking about that
emotion that I'm going to have

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:55.187
when the lights come on

00:00:55.187 --> 00:00:57.857
and I come out onstage
for the first time

00:00:57.857 --> 00:00:59.659
and I finally am back out there.

00:00:59.659 --> 00:01:01.360
I mean, I think we're --

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:02.761
You know, when you're --

00:01:02.761 --> 00:01:05.131
You've heard the term
kind of road dogs,

00:01:05.131 --> 00:01:09.034
and I've kind of always been a
guy that loves to be on the road

00:01:09.034 --> 00:01:12.104
and loves to be out there
with the fans and interacting.

00:01:12.104 --> 00:01:14.840
And, you know, the main thing
is, I just think about

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:18.110
that moment
when, you know, I hit the stage,

00:01:18.110 --> 00:01:20.913
and it's interesting.
I mean, I've even done some --

00:01:20.913 --> 00:01:23.716
You know, I've done
a couple Zoom concerts,

00:01:23.716 --> 00:01:25.184
and, I mean, I'm, like,

00:01:25.184 --> 00:01:27.921
forgetting the words to my songs
quite a bit.

00:01:27.921 --> 00:01:29.788
So I got to like -- I mean,

00:01:29.788 --> 00:01:31.757
I'm going to have to
sit in my music room

00:01:31.757 --> 00:01:33.826
and, like, go back
and listen to --

00:01:33.826 --> 00:01:36.262
Like, I'm going to have to
do a little extra prep,

00:01:36.262 --> 00:01:40.500
because I'm a little out of
practice on a lot of this stuff.

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:43.303
-A little rusty.
I will say that when we --

00:01:43.303 --> 00:01:46.205
We're lucky enough that we have
58 people in our audience,

00:01:46.205 --> 00:01:47.807
and they are as loud as --

00:01:47.807 --> 00:01:49.308
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:49.308 --> 00:01:51.544
They're as loud
as 10,000 people.

00:01:51.544 --> 00:01:53.713
And coming out --

00:01:53.713 --> 00:01:55.581
Coming out behind the stage

00:01:55.581 --> 00:01:59.185
and just seeing and hearing the
applause, it's emotional, buddy.

00:01:59.185 --> 00:02:00.453
It really is.

00:02:00.453 --> 00:02:02.522
-Yeah, it sounds like a big,
ol', full room in there.

00:02:02.522 --> 00:02:04.123
So, yeah, you got some --
You got some loud --

00:02:04.123 --> 00:02:05.357
-That's exactly right.

00:02:05.357 --> 00:02:08.027
This is New Yorkers, man.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:08.027 --> 00:02:11.564
Don't mess -- New Yorkers know
what's up, and they love you.

00:02:11.564 --> 00:02:13.465
-No one can yell
like New Yorkers, right?

00:02:13.465 --> 00:02:14.667
-No one in the world.

00:02:14.667 --> 00:02:16.335
There's no spirit like this.

00:02:16.335 --> 00:02:17.971
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:17.971 --> 00:02:20.006
-I have to say,
because, obviously,

00:02:20.006 --> 00:02:23.409
you couldn't be bigger and
more successful in your career,

00:02:23.409 --> 00:02:25.211
and everything is going great,

00:02:25.211 --> 00:02:27.880
and then you post
this Instagram post

00:02:27.880 --> 00:02:30.783
that made me laugh really hard,
and you said --

00:02:30.783 --> 00:02:32.218
Your quote was,
"I got to work harder."

00:02:32.218 --> 00:02:35.521
It's a picture of you
on some television show,

00:02:35.521 --> 00:02:38.591
but underneath you,
it says, "Blake Shelton."

00:02:38.591 --> 00:02:41.326
[ Laughter ]

00:02:41.326 --> 00:02:42.862
That's classic.

00:02:42.862 --> 00:02:44.931
Come on! You worked this hard.

00:02:44.931 --> 00:02:46.399
You have how many #1's?

00:02:46.399 --> 00:02:48.868
You're like,
"You think I'm Blake Shelton?"

00:02:48.868 --> 00:02:52.805
-That's former Sexiest Man Alive
right there on his couch.

00:02:52.805 --> 00:02:55.074
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:55.074 --> 00:02:56.642
-That's a good line.

00:02:56.642 --> 00:02:58.978
Obviously, you must know Blake.

00:02:58.978 --> 00:03:03.182
-Yeah, before I --
I think even before I --

00:03:03.182 --> 00:03:05.418
Before I even posted it
on Instagram,

00:03:05.418 --> 00:03:08.654
I sent -- I sent it to Blake,
and I'm like,

00:03:08.654 --> 00:03:11.891
"I mean, my life is pretty much
over after this point."

00:03:11.891 --> 00:03:13.392
[ Laughter ]

00:03:13.392 --> 00:03:16.362
You know, Blake just
chooses to go gray.

00:03:16.362 --> 00:03:21.433
You know, he just chooses to,
like, look like a silver fox.

00:03:21.433 --> 00:03:23.469
You know, I mean,
I got a lot "Just for Men"

00:03:23.469 --> 00:03:25.004
and hair products --
-Yes, exactly.

00:03:25.004 --> 00:03:26.339
You take care of yourself.
-And I work hard on this.

00:03:26.339 --> 00:03:27.840
-You work hard on this, exactly.

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:31.777
-And I can't even still -- I
still can't separate from Blake.

00:03:31.777 --> 00:03:33.946
It's just a shame.
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:33.946 --> 00:03:35.581
I want to talk about
"American Idol."

00:03:35.581 --> 00:03:37.116
You're fantastic on it, bud.

00:03:37.116 --> 00:03:39.252
And it's -- The whole crew is
great over there.

00:03:39.252 --> 00:03:41.687
I know that you had to miss
the first live show

00:03:41.687 --> 00:03:44.624
because of COVID, which must
have been scary for you.

00:03:44.624 --> 00:03:48.193
But, also, what was it like

00:03:48.193 --> 00:03:51.430
going through that
and also missing the shows?

00:03:51.430 --> 00:03:52.731
-Well, that's the fortunate --

00:03:52.731 --> 00:03:56.435
You know, like so many people
out there, it was --

00:03:56.435 --> 00:03:57.603
Like, I was one of those

00:03:57.603 --> 00:04:00.440
that, I mean, I was doing
as good as I could.

00:04:00.440 --> 00:04:02.408
Like, I really had done
a great job

00:04:02.408 --> 00:04:05.211
at, you know, masks
and all of that.

00:04:05.211 --> 00:04:08.013
And then to have that happen,
it was a bummer,

00:04:08.013 --> 00:04:11.317
and I was like, "Oh, gosh, this
is gonna be a media nightmare

00:04:11.317 --> 00:04:12.718
and I'm going to
have to miss stuff."

00:04:12.718 --> 00:04:14.954
But thankfully, you know,

00:04:14.954 --> 00:04:18.090
thankfully got through,
just, I kind of --

00:04:18.090 --> 00:04:21.059
Kind of quarantined myself off
in a part of the house.

00:04:21.059 --> 00:04:23.596
And it was pretty easy --

00:04:23.596 --> 00:04:26.766
You know, pretty easy to get
through as far as my symptoms.

00:04:26.766 --> 00:04:29.001
But certainly glad
I'm back in the chair now.

00:04:29.001 --> 00:04:30.402
I'm back rocking.

00:04:30.402 --> 00:04:33.272
And I love -- Love the show
this year, love the talent.

00:04:33.272 --> 00:04:35.107
I mean, you know, and even --

00:04:35.107 --> 00:04:37.009
I mean, we get
a little redundant.

00:04:37.009 --> 00:04:39.711
I mean, we keep saying, "Our
talent's better than last year,"

00:04:39.711 --> 00:04:42.881
but, you know, we --
We -- We've had producers,

00:04:42.881 --> 00:04:45.885
and we've had Seacrest,
who's been there since day one.

00:04:45.885 --> 00:04:49.755
I mean, he's pretty shocked
and amazed at the talent,

00:04:49.755 --> 00:04:51.190
and, you know, we feel like --

00:04:51.190 --> 00:04:52.524
You know,
we did a lot of auditions

00:04:52.524 --> 00:04:55.661
where the kids could
audition via Zoom

00:04:55.661 --> 00:04:58.597
and via just their computer,
and we felt like

00:04:58.597 --> 00:05:01.033
that brought a lot of talent
out of the woodworks,

00:05:01.033 --> 00:05:02.401
so it's been a great year.

00:05:02.401 --> 00:05:04.136
-You've been great
and very supportive.

00:05:04.136 --> 00:05:05.271
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:05:05.271 --> 00:05:06.939
Here's Luke Bryan on
"American Idol."

00:05:06.939 --> 00:05:08.107
Take a look at this.

00:05:08.107 --> 00:05:09.441
-Let's just walk
and you sing it.

00:05:09.441 --> 00:05:10.943
-Yeah, you know what?
-And we're just gonna walk it.

00:05:10.943 --> 00:05:12.211
-We won't look at you.
-Ready. Come on.

00:05:12.211 --> 00:05:13.279
-Yeah, ready?

00:05:13.279 --> 00:05:16.081
-♪ I got a girl crush ♪

00:05:16.081 --> 00:05:17.617
-Yes, you do.
-Yes, you do.

00:05:17.617 --> 00:05:21.921
-♪ Hate to admit it, but ♪

00:05:21.921 --> 00:05:26.058
♪ I got a hard rush ♪

00:05:26.058 --> 00:05:30.029
♪ It ain't slowin' down ♪
-Come on, now.

00:05:30.029 --> 00:05:31.063
-Give me a little bit
more frosting.

00:05:31.063 --> 00:05:33.732
-♪ I got a girl crush ♪

00:05:33.732 --> 00:05:34.767
-There it is.

00:05:34.767 --> 00:05:36.969
-The way you say crush
is magic.

00:05:36.969 --> 00:05:38.003
-Okay.
-Crush.

00:05:38.003 --> 00:05:39.638
-Crush.
-That's good!

00:05:39.638 --> 00:05:41.374
-Whoo!
-Alright.

00:05:41.374 --> 00:05:42.809
-Come on.

00:05:42.809 --> 00:05:44.209
That's what you want to see.

00:05:44.209 --> 00:05:47.580
Luke Bryan! "American Idol" airs
Sundays at 8:00 p.m. on ABC.

